  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A nucleus X emits a beta particle to produce a nucleus Y. If their atomic masses are $\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{x}}$ and $\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{y}}$ respectively, the maximum energy of the beta particle emitted is (where $m_{e}$ is the mass of an electron and $c$ is the velocity of light)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "vJfun",
      "text": "$\\left(\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{x}}-\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{y}}-\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{e}}\\right) \\mathrm{c}^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4PzbZ",
      "text": "$\\left(M_{x}-M_{y}+m_{e}\\right) \\mathrm{c}^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wTGXt",
      "text": "$\\left(M_{x}-M_{y}\\right) \\mathrm{c}^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "A4TMK",
      "text": "$\\left(M_{x}-M_{y}-2 m_{e}\\right) \\mathrm{c}^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint:\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/gKv3Gl__KGXJ4TL8YAEkwNsi4Jya45ra2uT2_xsXiuQ.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n$\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{x}}=\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{x}}-\\mathrm{zm}_{\\mathrm{e}}$\r\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{y}}=\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{y}}-(\\mathrm{z}+1) \\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{e}}}{\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{x}}-\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{y}}=\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{x}}-\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{y}}+\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{e}}}$\r\n$\\mathrm{E}=\\Delta \\mathrm{mC}^{2}=\\left(\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{x}}-\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{y}}-\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{e}}\\right) \\mathrm{C}^{2}=\\left(\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{x}}-\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{y}}\\right) \\mathrm{C}^{2}$",
    "image": null
